id: hate-empowerment
name: Hate Empowerment
order: 5
category: body
subrace: hatred-embodiment
importance: primary
description: >
  Empowered by the hatred you feel for those who destroyed your predecessors, you grow stronger as the fight wears on.
text: >
  Hate Empowerment (Body): Empowered by the hatred you feel for those who destroyed your predecessors, you grow stronger as the fight wears on.
  (1)-[Triggered, 1/Round]: If you spend 2+ Revenge Points on a single Attacking Maneuver that targets your Inferior, you may add an Energy Charge to that Attacking Maneuver.
  (2)-[Triggered]: Each time you spend Revenge Points, for every 2 Revenge Points spent, increase your Soak Value by 1(T) until the start of your next turn. The bonus to your Soak Value from this effect cannot exceed 4(T).
  (3)-[Triggered]: Gain 1 Revenge Point when you use the Power Up or Energy Charge Maneuver.
  (4)-[1/Round]: You may spend 2 Revenge Points to make a Basic Attack Maneuver as an Instant Maneuver. If you do, you must target your Inferior with this Attacking Maneuver.

---

[passive]
# (1) 2+ Revenge Points spent on an attack at this Round's Inferior: an Energy Charge, asked with them, once a Round
# (maneuvers.mjs askRevenge).
allow hate.charge;
# (2) Whatever spends them (chat.mjs spendRevenge): Hated (a mark), a stack for every 2, 1(T) of Soak each - 4 at most -
# each till the start of your next turn.
allow hate.soak;
# (4) The Basic Attack's Instant button on the Maneuvers tab, once a Round: 2 Revenge Points, at your Inferior alone.
allow hate.instant;

# (3) The Power Up or the Energy Charge Maneuver used. Automatic by default, its Triggered/Automatic button.
[triggered/declare-maneuver, toggle, effect 3]
requires using("power-up") || using("energy-charge");
revengepoints.stacks += 1;
